WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.740
Amazon has yet another massive hit on its
hands in the form of "Reacher."

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.360
The series has given audiences a towering
new action hero to look up to.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.070
The 1st season of "Reacher" proved an immediate
success for the streaming service, following

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:15.820
the former soldier as a drifter who finds
himself embroiled in a criminal conspiracy

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.320
in a small Georgia town.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.119
The show has proven so successful, in fact,
that it's already been greenlit for a 2nd

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:22.119
season.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.730
"Trouble just kinda seems to find me."

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.980
The soldier-turned-detective at the heart
of "Reacher" might look familiar to fans of

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:27.980
the series.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.830
That's because the action hero is portrayed
by Alan Ritchson, an actor with a career full

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.590
of great performances in the world of action
and comedy.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.500
With "Reacher" becoming the monumental hit
that it is, and with more action on the way,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.100
now is the time to dive in and take a look
at some of the most notable roles and performances

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.620
that fans may know Alan Ritchson from over
the years.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.300
One of the first major on-screen roles that
many audience members may recognize Alan Ritchson

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.670
from is his role as Arthur "AC" Curry in "Smallville."

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.830
Introduced to the show during Season 5 in
2005, Ritchson would go on to appear on The

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:00.320
WB's Superman prequel series four times until
2010.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.140
"You're not going anywhere."

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:14.560
The popularity of the Aquaman character on
"Smallville" eventually led to a planned spinoff

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.560
for the character.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.780
However, when the "Aquaman" series went to
pilot, Ritchson was ultimately recast.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.590
Despite not playing Aquaman in live-action
outside of his tenure on "Smallville," Ritchson

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.860
would eventually go on to reprise his Aquaman
role in voiceover for the animated film, "Justice

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.270
League: The New Frontier," in 2008.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.780
Alan Ritchson has played several athletes
over the course of his career, but perhaps

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.060
his most well-known athlete performance is
his role as Thad Castle in the Spike TV comedy

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.759
series "Blue Mountain State."

00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:43.800
Though initially pitched as a soft antagonist
who bullied and hazed his teammates, Thad

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.970
eventually became the co-lead of the series
in the show's 2nd and 3rd seasons.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.979
Outside of his work in the DC and "Reacher"
universes, Thad Castle may arguably be one

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:55.460
of Ritchson's defining performances as an
actor.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.040
"Cocaine.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.200
Yeah baby."

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.579
In 2016, Ritchson reprised the role of Thad
in earnest for the "Blue Mountain State" spinoff

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:06.490
movie: "Blue Mountain State: The Rise of Thadland."

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.479
Another high-profile film series where you
might have caught Ritchson was "The Hunger

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:10.479
Games."

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:14.191
He portrayed Gloss, one of the most gifted
and talented tributes in the games.

00:02:14.191 --> 00:02:18.610
A career combatant from District 1 who specialized
in throwing knives, Gloss battled Katniss

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.500
and the other returning winners in "The Hunger
Games: Catching Fire," alongside his sister

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.500
Cashmere.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.510
Ritchson's tenure in "The Hunger Games" franchise
was ultimately short-lived.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.730
If "Blue Mountain State" proved he could catch
a football, "The Hunger Games" showed he was

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:32.550
just as good at doing it with arrows.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.000
But even though Gloss went down, Ritchson
was going nowhere but up in Hollywood.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.110
After putting in a few cameos in popular shows
like "New Girl," Ritchson landed one of the

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:45.780
leads in a very different type of comic adaptation:
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.570
Although you couldn't see his face, he provided
the voice and motion capture for Raphael.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.620
"Actually I'm in charge on this one."

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.920
In 2018, Alan Ritchson found himself back
in the DC universe in the role of Hank Hall,

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.650
a.k.a Hawk, in "Titans."

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:02.790
A former football player who eventually became
a vigilante, Hank was a brutal fighter who

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.320
patrolled the streets in a Hawk-themed outfit.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:10.100
He was one half of the "Hawk and Dove" crime-fighting
duo, balancing out the more nuanced and finesse-oriented

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.710
fighting style of Dove with a brute force
approach.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:17.290
As Hawk, Ritchson would make several appearances
across various DC properties.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:21.260
In addition to his primary role on "Titans,"
he also briefly appeared on "Supergirl" during

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.280
the "Crisis on Infinite Earths" crossover
event.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.320
Unfortunately for Hawk, the character ultimately
met his demise during "Titans" Season 3.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.500
Ritchson has continued to appear on "Titans"
in sequences following Hank into the afterlife,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.320
but at this time, the character remains canonically
dead.

